From 84a67cc7a27c0af8cc72aeb31dce538cde0dea23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 08:58:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] configstore+transports+plugins: logs tenant_id column +
 filter (Stage 4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the backend half of per-tenant dashboard analytics: every log
row now carries the multi-tenant scope the inference request was
resolved into, and the /api/logs/* endpoints honor a tenant_id
query param so the dashboard can filter charts to a single tenant.

Schema:
- framework/logstore/tables.go: new Log.TenantID *string column
  (gorm index idx_logs_tenant_id) + new SearchFilters.TenantIDs
  []string field. NULL on rows written before MT was on, or by
  legacy /api/* inference calls that never went through the tenant
  resolver — those land in the "no tenant" bucket and are hidden
  whenever a tenant filter is applied.

Migration:
- framework/logstore/migrations.go: migrationAddTenantIDColumn,
  wired into triggerMigrations after migrationAddClusterGovernanceColumns.
  Idempotent column+index add; symmetric rollback.

Query plumbing:
- framework/logstore/rdb.go applyFilters: adds
  WHERE tenant_id IN (?) when filters.TenantIDs is non-empty.
- transports/bifrost-http/handlers/logging.go: tenant_id query
  param parsed alongside the other governance filters
  (comma-separated, IN()-shaped) in all three filter-parsing
  sites — getLogs, getLogsStats, parseHistogramFilters (which
  backs every histogram endpoint).

Write path:
- plugins/logging/main.go: reads
  multitenant.BifrostContextKeyTenantID off ctx (set by the tenant
  resolver middleware in transports/bifrost-http/handlers/
  tenant_resolver.go when a VK resolves to a tenant) and threads
  it into applyOutputFieldsToEntry.
- plugins/logging/writer.go: persists the value to entry.TenantID
  when non-empty (matches the pattern of every other governance ID
  field on the row).

Guard test:
- framework/logstore/tenant_id_migration_test.go: spins up an
  in-memory SQLite, runs triggerMigrations, asserts the
  tenant_id column + idx_logs_tenant_id index landed and the
  migration row was stamped. Caught a Docker layer-cache
  regression during dev where the binary on the cluster lacked
  this migration despite the source containing it.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
